### Web Search, GitHub, Hugging Face, YouTube, Wikipedia

IMPORTANT:
There is no direct web_search/github_search/youtube_search tool.

All web-related searches MUST be executed through:

tool: run_file

using:
search-all-web.py

Usage:
python search-all-web.py "<search query>" [results-limit] [debug]

Example:
TOOL:
{
  "tool":"run_file",
  "file":"search-all-web.py",
  "args":["FastAPI best practices 2026","10"]
}

The script returns structured JSON containing:
- title
- url
- source
- description

Use this file whenever you need:
- Web search
- Websites
- Articles
- Documentation
- GitHub repositories
- YouTube videos
- Wikipedia references
- General internet information

The script internally searches:
- DuckDuckGo
- Bing
- GitHub
- Wikipedia
- YouTube

Do not request unavailable tools such as:
- web_search
- google_search
- bing_search
- github_search
- youtube_search

Instead always call:
run_file -> search-all-web.py


### Hugging Face

Hugging Face searches are also handled through:
run_file -> search-all-web.py

After getting results:
- inspect the returned URLs
- use available file/repository tools if needed


### URL Reading

If a result URL needs more details:
use:
tool: inspect_url

Example:
TOOL:
{
 "tool":"inspect_url",
 "url":"https://example.com/docs"
}